  "_readme": [
    "Author attributions, kept separate from the extracted text so that re-running",
    "scripts/extract-hymns.mjs never overwrites research. The hymnal itself prints",
    "no authors at all, so every entry here comes from outside the book and is",
    "matched by first line — the stable key for public-domain hymnody, since these",
    "titles are the Brethren editors' topical labels rather than the hymns' names.",
    "",
    "Only well-documented authorship is claimed. Hymns that are anonymous, are",
    "centos assembled from several writers (hymn 1 is Watts plus Tate and Brady),",
    "or are Brethren-specific texts of uncertain origin are deliberately absent and",
    "render as unattributed. Absence here means 'not established', not 'anonymous'.",
    "'How firm a foundation' (523-524) is a case in point: it is signed only 'K—'",
    "in Rippon's Selection, and Keene, Keith and Kirkham have all been proposed.",
    "",
    "source: 'hymnary.org' was checked directly against that entry.",
    "source: 'standard hymnody reference' is settled, widely published authorship",
    "that was not individually re-verified against a primary source."
  ]
}
